{
  "info": {
    "name": "Beta Platform — Integration API (v1)",
    "_postman_id": "b3ta0005-1nt3-4a91-9v01-c0llect10n05",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Integration API for the Beta Platform: sign in for a bearer token, renew it with a refresh token, read and add products, and raise a work order.\n\n## Start here\n1. Set `baseUrl` (default `http://localhost:5045`, the app's default launch profile).\n2. Set `adminEmail` / `adminPassword`.\n3. Run **1 · Auth → Sign in**. It stores `{{accessToken}}` and `{{refreshToken}}`; every other request picks the access token up automatically.\n4. When the access token expires, run **Renew tokens** instead of signing in again.\n\nAccess tokens last **8 hours**; refresh tokens last **30 days** and are **rotated** on every renewal — the response always carries a new one, and the old one should be discarded.\n\n## One request per endpoint\nThis collection contains only the six operations, each on its happy path. The failure cases — wrong password, missing token, wrong role, malformed body, unknown code — are specified in `contracts/` and exercised deliberately in `quickstart.md`; they are not requests you want to run by accident with **Run collection**.\n\n## Products are addressed by CODE\nNo internal record number appears anywhere in this API, in either direction. A work order names its input and output products by the code the plant prints and files by — **several inputs, one output**: `inputProductCodes` is a list (at least one entry, none blank, no code twice), `outputProductCode` is a single code. An unresolvable input code is answered by a 400 naming its position, `inputProductCodes[i]`.\n\n## ⚠️ Contract-first slice\nAuthentication, permissions and request validation are **fully implemented**. The product and work-order operations return **representative data and persist nothing** — so creating the same product code twice answers 201 twice, because there is no stored catalogue to conflict with. The 409 for a duplicate is specified in the contract and starts being produced when the behaviour slice lands, with no change to any URL, body, header or status code.\n\nLive document: `{{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json` · Interactive reference: `{{baseUrl}}/docs`"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5045",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Default launch profile. Use https://localhost:7017 for the https profile, or http://localhost:5000 with --no-launch-profile."
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@beta.local",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "Admin@123",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The development seed password. Replace for any real environment."
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Set automatically by Sign in and by Renew tokens. 8-hour life."
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Set automatically by Sign in and rotated by Renew tokens. 30-day life. As secret as the password it stands in for."
    },
    {
      "key": "workOrderNumber",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Generated per request by a pre-request script."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 · Contract",
      "description": "The published document itself — not part of the API surface, but the first thing an integrator reads.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "OpenAPI document",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "openapi",
                "v1.json"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "The machine-readable contract (FR-032). You can import this URL into Postman directly if you would rather generate requests than use this collection."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const doc = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('describes all six operations', () => {",
                  "  const ops = Object.values(doc.paths).reduce((n, p) => n + Object.keys(p).length, 0);",
                  "  pm.expect(ops).to.eql(6);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('declares the bearer scheme', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(doc.components.securitySchemes).to.have.property('bearerAuth'));",
                  "pm.test('carries the slice note', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(doc.info.description).to.include('SLICE NOTE'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1 · Auth",
      "description": "Fully implemented — a real account, a real password check, a real token.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign in  ▶ saves {{accessToken}} + {{refreshToken}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Stores both tokens as collection variables. The access token lasts 8 hours; when it expires run **Renew tokens** rather than sending the password again."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.refreshToken);",
                  "pm.test('returns a bearer token', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(b.tokenType).to.eql('Bearer');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('returns a refresh token', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(b.refreshToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "pm.test('expires ~8 hours out', () => {",
                  "  const hours = (new Date(b.expiresAt) - new Date()) / 3600000;",
                  "  pm.expect(hours).to.be.within(7.9, 8.1);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('the refresh token outlives it', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(new Date(b.refreshTokenExpiresAt)).to.be.above(new Date(b.expiresAt)));",
                  "pm.test('reports the account roles', () => pm.expect(b.roles).to.include('Admin'));",
                  "console.log('Tokens stored. Access expires ' + b.expiresAt + ', refresh ' + b.refreshTokenExpiresAt);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Renew tokens  ▶ rotates {{refreshToken}}",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "description": "Exchanges the refresh token for a fresh pair — no password, and no access token required (the caller's may well have expired, which is the point).\n\nRenewal **rotates**: the response carries a new refresh token and this request stores it over the old one. Roles and the account's active state are re-read from the platform, so a deactivated account or a changed password stops renewals immediately rather than at the 30-day expiry."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "const presented = JSON.parse(pm.request.body.raw).refreshToken;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.refreshToken);",
                  "pm.test('returns a new access token', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(b.tokenType).to.eql('Bearer');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('rotates the refresh token', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(b.refreshToken).to.not.eql(presented));",
                  "pm.test('the new access token is good for another ~8 hours', () => {",
                  "  const hours = (new Date(b.expiresAt) - new Date()) / 3600000;",
                  "  pm.expect(hours).to.be.within(7.9, 8.1);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('answers in the same shape sign-in does', () => {",
                  "  ['accessToken','tokenType','expiresAt','refreshToken','refreshTokenExpiresAt','email','fullName','roles']",
                  "    .forEach(k => pm.expect(b).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('Renewed. Access expires ' + b.expiresAt + ', refresh ' + b.refreshTokenExpiresAt);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 · Products",
      "description": "Shapes final; the data behind them is representative in this slice.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List products",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "products"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "activeOnly",
                  "value": "true",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Enable to exclude deactivated products. Part of the agreed contract even while it filters representative data."
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Any authenticated caller. An empty catalogue is `[]`, never a 404. Enable the `activeOnly` query parameter to filter."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('returns an array', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "pm.test('no product id anywhere (FR-022)', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text().toLowerCase()).to.not.include('productid'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get product by code",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/RM-STEEL-01",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "products",
                "RM-STEEL-01"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Addressed by product code. Codes are trimmed and matched case-insensitively, so `rm-steel-01` and `  RM-Steel-01  ` reach the same product."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const p = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('carries the full product shape', () => {",
                  "  ['productCode','productName','productNameEnglish','category','unit','isActive']",
                  "    .forEach(k => pm.expect(p).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('no product id anywhere (FR-022)', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text().toLowerCase()).to.not.include('productid'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create product (Admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "products"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productCode\": \"RM-NEW-{{$randomInt}}\",\n  \"productName\": \"منتج جديد\",\n  \"productNameEnglish\": \"New Product\",\n  \"category\": \"Raw Material\",\n  \"unit\": \"kg\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Admin only. Validated and permission-checked for real; NOT persisted in this slice. Note there is no isActive field to send — a created product is always active (FR-017)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('Location addresses it by CODE, not an id', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.include('/api/v1/products/'));",
                  "pm.test('created active', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().isActive).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('no product id anywhere (FR-022)', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text().toLowerCase()).to.not.include('productid'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 · Work orders",
      "description": "The feature's end goal: an order whose inputs and output are named by product code \u2014 a list of input codes, one output code.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create work order",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/work-orders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "work-orders"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"workOrderNumber\": \"{{workOrderNumber}}\",\n  \"inputProductCodes\": [\"RM-STEEL-01\", \"RM-PAINT-02\"],\n  \"outputProductCode\": \"FG-PANEL-07\",\n  \"plannedStartTime\": \"2026-09-01T06:00:00\",\n  \"qtyToManufacture\": 1200.5,\n  \"machineId\": 3,\n  \"hourRate\": 45.0,\n  \"lineSetupTimeMinutes\": 30,\n  \"workstationCapabilityPerHour\": 150.0\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Admin or Client. Inputs are a LIST of product codes (at least one, none blank, no repeats); the output is a single code. machineId is the one internal identifier that remains one — machines have no external code on this surface."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('workOrderNumber', 'WO-' + Date.now());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const w = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('echoes every code exactly as submitted, inputs in order', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(w.inputProductCodes).to.eql(['RM-STEEL-01', 'RM-PAINT-02']);",
                  "  pm.expect(w.outputProductCode).to.eql('FG-PANEL-07');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('status is the NAME Ready, not an enum integer', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(w.status).to.eql('Ready'));",
                  "pm.test('no product id anywhere (FR-022)', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text().toLowerCase()).to.not.include('productid'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
